The comment "@@@ Each collection element appears one index later in the returned array." seems to be incorrect based on the implementation of the `toArray()` method. The `toArray()` method actually copies the elements starting from index 0 in the returned array, not one index later.

However, if we assume the comment is meant to specify that the returned array has the same elements in the same order as the list, then the correct assert statement would be:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.get(i).equals(((Object[]) \result)[i]);</code>

This asserts that each element in the list is equal to the corresponding element in the returned array.
